{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108227","id":2637234998,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6dMQM2","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108227","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108227.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108227.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108227","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108227/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108227/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108227/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/9ad608691b2f06727e647dfea8f7b58051ca6916","number":108227,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Propagate `Tween.kill()` to subtweens","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR fixes a problem with tween/subtween logic I noticed while investigating another issue. Previously, when a tween was killed with `kill()`, if it had subtweens in it that hadn't yet been run, those subtweens would never be executed, but would also never be explicitly killed or made invalid. As a result, if user code was monitoring the status of a subtween (say, waiting for it to be killed or finished), they would end up waiting forever.\r\n\r\nWith this PR, a `kill()` call on a Tween is passed down to all of its subtweens as well, ensuring that they are all marked as dead/invalid.\n\n>[!NOTE]\n> Previously this PR also cleared subtweens when `clear()` was called on the parent. As I thought it through more I realized this didn't make sense, so I removed that but kept the `kill()` behavior.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"http